page=head+'''<title>Hicham Halfi | Machine Learning &amp; AI Engineering</title><meta name="description" content="Hicham Halfi's portfolio: applied machine learning, RAG systems, multi-agent research, and reproducible validation."><meta property="og:title" content="Hicham Halfi — Machine Learning & AI Engineering"><meta property="og:description" content="Practical AI systems, with the evidence and limitations behind them."><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://hicham-halfi.github.io/Intern-Flyrank/assets/validation_comparison.png"></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header><a class="brand" href="./">Hicham Halfi<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#work">Work</a><a href="#about">About</a><a href="cv.html">CV</a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/hicham-halfi/">LinkedIn</a></nav></header><main id="main"><div class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Machine Learning / Data Science / AI Engineering</p><h1>I build AI systems.<br>Then test what<br>they really know.</h1><p class="intro">I'm Hicham, a machine learning engineer based in Marrakech. My work spans applied ML, retrieval-augmented generation, and multi-agent decision systems.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="#work">Explore my work ↓</a><a class="button" href="https://github.com/hicham-halfi">GitHub ↗</a><a class="button" href="cv.html">Read my CV ↗</a></div></div><section id="work"><p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p><h2>From an encouraging score<br>to a defensible result.</h2><article class="feature"><div><p class="tag">FlyRank / Reproducible ML audit</p><h3>Content decline, without the easy answers</h3><p><strong>Problem:</strong> a content editor needs a review queue they can trust.</p><p><strong>What I did:</strong> reproduced a forest model, separated clients across train and test, audited feature timing, and built a playbook with explicit human approval rules.</p><p><strong>What came of it:</strong> the original feature set's Precision@20 changed from 90% to 50% after client separation. The finding is retrospective; it does not promise future accuracy or traffic lift.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="../">Read the research ↗</a><a class="button" href="https://github.com/hicham-halfi/Intern-Flyrank">Inspect the code ↗</a></div></div><img src="../assets/validation_comparison.png" width="1620" height="810" alt="The original model's top-20 precision drops from 90 percent on random rows to 50 percent on held-out clients."></article><div class="projects"><article class="project"><p class="tag">Research / Multi-agent reinforcement learning</p><h3>Vehicles as cooperating agents</h3><p>At Ecole Centrale Casablanca, I worked on capacity-constrained vehicle routing by modeling vehicles and depots as agents, with reinforcement learning for decentralized decisions and communication for coordination.</p><p class="small">PFE research internship · March–July 2025 · Experience described in my CV; no public benchmark result is claimed here.</p></article><article class="project"><p class="tag">LLMs / Retrieval / Data pipelines</p><h3>A retail digital twin</h3><p>During my Digiole training, I worked on an LLM and vector-database assistant for Mall of Tripla, alongside Python collection pipelines and NLP analysis of unstructured feedback.</p><p class="small">Remote training · September 2025–February 2026 · Experience described in my CV; client data and internal artifacts are not published.</p></article></div></section><section id="demo"><p class="eyebrow">Try a small working tool</p><h2>Plan an editorial review budget.</h2><p>This is a planning calculator inspired by the action playbook. Change the assumptions to see what fits; it does not estimate traffic returns or choose which pages to publish.</p><form class="planner" id="budget-form"><div class="fields"><div><label for="budget">Total budget ($)</label><input id="budget" name="budget" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" step="0.01" value="300" required></div><div><label for="rate">Editor rate ($/hour)</label><input id="rate" name="rate" type="number" min="0.01" max="100000" step="0.01" value="30" required></div><div><label for="effort">Review time (hours/page)</label><input id="effort" name="effort" type="number" min="0.01" max="1000" step="0.01" value="1" required></div></div><button type="submit">Calculate review capacity</button><output id="budget-result" for="budget rate effort" aria-live="polite">Enter your assumptions and calculate.</output><p class="small">Runs entirely in your browser. Values are not sent or stored. Human review and content decisions stay with you.</p></form></section><section id="about"><p class="eyebrow">Background</p><h2>Research curiosity.<br>Practical engineering.</h2><p>My master's work at FSTG Marrakech focused on vehicle-routing optimization through multi-agent reinforcement learning. I enjoy turning an open-ended AI problem into a narrow system, a reproducible experiment, and a clear explanation of its limits.</p><div class="experience"><p class="small">July–September 2026</p><div><h3>AI Engineering Intern · FlyRank AI</h3><p>Part-time, remote. Work on generative-AI analysis workflows, NLP processing and practical AI systems.</p></div></div><div class="experience"><p class="small">September 2025–February 2026</p><div><h3>Machine Learning Trainee · Digiole</h3><p>LLM/RAG assistance, Python data pipelines and NLP analysis.</p></div></div><div class="experience"><p class="small">March–July 2025</p><div><h3>Data Science Research Intern · Ecole Centrale</h3><p>Multi-agent reinforcement learning for vehicle-routing problems.</p></div></div><h3>Tools I work with</h3><div class="skills"><span>Python</span><span>SQL</span><span>scikit-learn</span><span>PyTorch</span><span>TensorFlow</span><span>LangChain</span><span>FastAPI</span><span>Git</span></div></section><section id="notes"><p class="eyebrow">Research notes</p><h2>What changed when I changed the test?</h2><p>My latest note follows the content-decline model from its original random split to client-held-out evaluation, including the errors and the result that did not survive.</p><a href="../">Read the full note ↗</a></section><section id="contact"><p class="eyebrow">Let's connect</p><h2>Have a problem worth testing?</h2><p>Find my professional background on LinkedIn or explore the reproducible work on GitHub.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/hicham-halfi/">Connect on LinkedIn ↗</a><a class="button" href="https://github.com/hicham-halfi">Explore GitHub ↗</a><a class="button" href="cv.html">CV ↗</a></div></section></main><footer>© 2026 Hicham Halfi · Built with plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript · Research data credit: <a href="https://flyrank.ai">FlyRank</a></footer><script src="planner.js"></script></body></html>'''
